  "comments": [
    {
      "texts": [
        {
          "evidences": [
            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250",
              "source": "UniProtKB",
              "id": "Q72SM7"
            },
            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "11953365"
            },
            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "19103763"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Major outer membrane lipoprotein present exclusively in pathogenic Leptospira species (PubMed:11953365, PubMed:19103763). It displays high immunogenicity (By similarity). LipL32 is not required for either acute or chronic models of infection, suggesting that it does not play an indispensable role in pathogenesis (PubMed:19103763). It is also not required for survival in water (PubMed:19103763). It may be important in the transmission or environmental survival phase of the life cycle, or be necessary for a function not detected by the animal models used (PubMed:19103763)"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "FUNCTION"
    },
    {
      "texts": [
        {
          "evidences": [
            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "20510346"
            }
          ],
          "value": "When administered to culture with human umbilical vein endothelial cells (HUVEC), LipL32 can increase the cellular permeability of HUVECs, induce reorganization and up-regulation of F-actin, down-regulate the expression of the tight junction protein 1 (TJP1/ZO1) and induce apoptosis of the HUVEC"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "FUNCTION"
    },
    {
      "texts": [
        {
          "evidences": [
            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "11953365"
            }
          ],
          "value": "LipL32 undergoes a number of iron-dependent proteolytic cleavage events in vitro (PubMed:11953365). The cleavage may be biologically significant and more than one process may be involved (PubMed:11953365)"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "ACTIVITY REGULATION"
    },
    {
      "texts": [
        {
          "evidences": [
            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "19236879"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Homodimer"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "SUBUNIT"
    },
    {
      "commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION",
      "note": {
        "texts": [
          {
            "evidences": [
              {
                "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250",
                "source": "UniProtKB",
                "id": "Q72SM7"
              }
            ],
            "value": "Was identified as a surface-exposed outer membrane lipoprotein. However, one study shows that the protein is not detected on the surface of intact cells by immunofluorescence assay (IFA), but becomes accessible to antibodies only after permeabilization of the outer membrane, suggesting that LipL32 is not exposed on the surface, but that it may be a sub-surface membrane lipoprotein on the inner leaflet of the outer membrane"
          }
        ]
      },
      "subcellularLocations": [
        {
          "location": {
            "evidences": [
              {
                "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
                "source": "PubMed",
                "id": "11953365"
              }
            ],
            "value": "Cell outer membrane",
            "id": "SL-0040"
          },
          "topology": {
            "evidences": [
              {
                "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255",
                "source": "PROSITE-ProRule",
                "id": "PRU00303"
              }
            ],
            "value": "Lipid-anchor",
            "id": "SL-9901"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "texts": [
        {
          "evidences": [
            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "19236879"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Possesses a compact globular jelly-roll fold with a number of surface-exposed features that indicate a potential capacity to bind other components or interact with itself"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "DOMAIN"
    },
    {
      "texts": [
        {
          "evidences": [
            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "19103763"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Can be deleted, is not essential for the survival of L.interrogans (PubMed:19103763). The mutant has normal morphology and growth rate compared to the wild type and is equally adherent to extracellular matrix (PubMed:19103763). The mutant causes severe disease manifestations in the hamster model of acute infection and it colonizes the renal tubules as efficiently as the wild-type strain in the rat model of chronic infection (PubMed:19103763)"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "DISRUPTION PHENOTYPE"
    },
    {
      "texts": [
        {
          "evidences": [
            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Belongs to the LipL32 family"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "SIMILARITY"
    }
  ],
